---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="AI Audio Report is a small independent publication covering what music-production software costs and what its licences permit, with every fact dated and sourced."
>
  <h1 class="page-title">About AI Audio Report</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    A small independent publication about the software musicians and audio people pay for:
    what it costs, what the licence actually permits, and which option fits the job.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    Search for almost any AI audio tool and you will get three kinds of page: the vendor's own
    blog explaining why its product won the comparison it ran, an affiliate round-up whose
    prices were accurate eighteen months ago, and a post that confidently answers a legal
    question by guessing. We checked. The prices in those pages contradict each other, and
    several of the licensing answers are flatly out of date, because the terms were rewritten
    underneath them.
  </p>
  <p>
    None of that is hard to beat. It just requires doing the boring part: opening the actual
    pricing page, reading the actual terms, writing down the date, and linking to both.
  </p>

  <h2>What we are good for, and what we are not</h2>
  <p>
    Good for: current prices with a verification date, what a licence permits read from the
    source document, cost arithmetic nobody else bothers to do, and picking between options
    for a specific situation.
  </p>
  <p>
    Not good for: how something sounds. We do not test hardware or run listening tests, and we
    will not pretend to. For that, go to people who do it properly, and we will link to them
    when their judgement is what matters. The
    <a href={withBase('/editorial-policy/')}>editorial policy</a> spells all of this out,
    including our use of AI in research and drafting.
  </p>

  <h2>Who writes it</h2>
  <p>
    AI Audio Report is run and edited by <strong>Arnau Gran i Romero</strong>. Writing carries a
    <strong>AI Audio Report editorial team</strong> byline, and articles he has personally read
    and checked name him as reviewer. One person, named, rather than a masthead of experts
    the site does not have.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>
    No advertising, no sponsored content, and at the moment no affiliate links and no revenue
    at all. If that changes, it gets disclosed on every page it touches. The
    <a href={withBase('/affiliate-disclosure/')}>rules are published in advance</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Corrections, tip-offs and “your price is wrong” emails are all welcome:
    <a href={withBase('/contact/')}>contact us</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
